                        "entry_id": "fcf2454e-c2ea-3421-8283-7bc2bc9ad0a4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "postawa polegająca na pozytywnym stosunku do Żydów i kultury żydowskiej"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "09260218-0a17-4fc2-94b2-5612a41bc700",
                                "sense_id": "2ea3fce6-2349-304c-a7ed-0644fe2cc26c",
                                "text": "Wysłuchaliśmy wykładu na temat filosemityzmu polskich monarchów."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "505366c8-0512-4f32-98fb-5e8e10bdf7f2",
                        "source_entry_id": "fcf2454e-c2ea-3421-8283-7bc2bc9ad0a4",
                        "source_sense_id": "2ea3fce6-2349-304c-a7ed-0644fe2cc26c",
                        "target_lang_word": "philo-Semitism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "philo-Semitism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43c85039-5d0b-36c1-be45-900a2f0114cd",
                                        "entry_id": "3dab9c8b-9ad7-367e-90d3-b97abfdebfa2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Interest in or appreciation of Jewish people, their history, or the influence of Judaism, particularly on the part of a gentile."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93a2142b-f2d2-41f3-ae26-8694a39fcd09",
                                                "sense_id": "43c85039-5d0b-36c1-be45-900a2f0114cd",
                                                "text": "To an Englishman, German liberalism is a hybrid creature, lame of three legs and blind of one eye, and thus it is necessary to explain — if indeed explanation in its rational sense be possible — the position of the German Liberals in this matter of philo-Semitism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1424266-2130-4c4d-9302-0765df91ccf5",
                                                "sense_id": "43c85039-5d0b-36c1-be45-900a2f0114cd",
                                                "text": "The new civilizationism is a paradoxical combination of “identitarian” Christianity, secularism, philo-Semitism, Islamophobia, and even some elements of liberalism such as support for gender equality and gay rights."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1714a0a-4664-42f7-92f3-83819df87faa",
                                                "sense_id": "43c85039-5d0b-36c1-be45-900a2f0114cd",
                                                "text": "The great sociologist Zygmunt Bauman argued that philo-Semitism and anti-Semitism both fall under “allosemitism”: literally Othering the Jew. He defined it not as resentment of what is different, which is xenophobia, but rather of what defies order and clear categories. In 1997, he wrote, “The Jew is ambivalence incarnate. And ambivalence is ambivalence mostly because it cannot be contemplated without ambivalent feeling: it is simultaneously attractive and repelling.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
